label idiots
[signal arg="bg:library_evening"]
Enriko: Okay, hypothetically, if each of us had to marry one professor at this academy, purely for the storytelling value, who's it going to be?
Veldero: That is not a hypothetical anyone needs.
Enriko: It's an excellent hypothetical. Lan, back me up.
Lan (Smug): Depends. Does the marriage come with tenure, or do I have to attend the wedding in full academy uniform?
Enriko: Obviously full uniform. Nobody negotiates their way out of the uniform.
Lan (Smug): Then I withdraw entirely. I've seen what happens to people who commit to a look for the aesthetic alone.
Enriko: Fine, I'll go first. Adelaide. Terrifying, brilliant, and I have a theory she secretly finds me delightful under all that scolding.
Veldero: You have a theory about everyone finding you delightful.
Lan (Smug): It is genuinely never correct.
Enriko: Your turn, Veldero. And it has to be a real answer, not "Instructor Amir, because I fear him," like last time.
Veldero: Fear is simply respect with better instincts.
Enriko: Lan, you're being suspiciously quiet.
- "Doc. Free tea, doesn't ask questions."
	Lan (Smug): Doc. Free tea, doesn't ask questions, wouldn't notice if I missed a class for a month.
	Enriko: That's not a real answer, that's a description of your ideal landlord.
	Lan (Smug): I contain multitudes.
- "I don't have a favorite."
	Lan (Default): I don't have a favorite.
	Veldero: That's exactly what someone with a favorite says.
	Lan (Smug): I contain multitudes.
They sat like that for a while, three people who'd stopped needing every silence filled.
Veldero: You ever miss home?
Enriko: Sometimes. My family's loud.
Enriko: Too many cousins, too many business dinners where somebody's trying to marry me off for trade reasons.
Enriko: It's a good kind of loud.
Enriko: I miss it the way you miss a noise that used to keep you awake and now the quiet keeps you up instead.
Lan (Sus): (A porch. A father who split logs without ever explaining why. A family who waved me off smiling like exile was the happiest day of their lives.)
- "Sometimes. It's complicated."
	set {aff_veldero} += 1
	Lan (Default): Sometimes. It's complicated. I don't think I'd go back even if I could, but that's not the same as not missing it.
	Something shifted in Veldero's face at that, recognition maybe, before he covered it with the easy smile everyone knew him by.
	Veldero: Yeah. I miss it more than I let on. There are people back there I think about a lot. More than I'd expect, this far in.
- "Not really."
	Lan (Default): Not really. I try not to.
	Veldero: Lucky.
Enriko: Careful. That almost sounded sincere. I don't know what to do with sincere Veldero.
Veldero: I'll never do it again, I promise.
Lan (Smug): Their haircuts are terrible, though.
Veldero: Objectively terrible.
label spar
[signal arg="bg:east_wing_night"]
Dialog/Ilia (Goof): Evening, my secret little swordsman. Evening, Liesel. I brought you something. Don't tell anyone, it's against at least two academy rules.
Liesel (Flat): Bribery.
Dialog/Ilia (Goof): Friendship, technically, but I understand the confusion.
She drew her rapier, took her stance, and the whole room changed.
One second she was laughing about a bun's questionable filling, and the next her eyes had gone flat and focused and entirely still.
Dialog/Ilia (Def): Ready?
Lan (Combat): Ready.
[signal arg="combat:spar_ilia"]
She came in fast, a blur of thrusts testing his guard from three angles before he'd registered the first.
Every attack came from a slightly different line, forcing him to solve it fresh each time.
Dialog/Ilia (Def): Dead. You leave the same half-second gap every time you commit to a full arc.
Dialog/Ilia (Def): Big weapon, big commitment, and I only need the half-second you're stuck inside it.
Lan (Smug): Noted. Again?
Dialog/Ilia (Happy): Obviously again. This is the most fun I've had in months. Please don't ever get better at closing that gap. I'd miss it.
set {stat_sword} += 1
set {aff_ilia} += 1
They went four more rounds, and Lan lost three of the four, cleanly and honestly,
and walked away from every loss feeling more like himself than he had in weeks.
Dialog/Ilia (Goof): Same time Thursday?
Lan (Smile): Same time Thursday.
label staying
Liesel (Default): I've been thinking about the arrangement. The party was one class. You never actually asked whether I intended to keep showing up after it ended.
Liesel (Default): I've decided I'm going to. Not because you asked again. You didn't, which is probably why I'm telling you now.
Liesel (Default): I'd rather choose it than be recruited into it twice.
Lan (Default): I wasn't going to ask again. I didn't want to push.
Liesel (Smile): I noticed. It's part of why I'm agreeing. For the record, Schwert, you're stuck with me now. Officially.
- "Wouldn't dream of talking you out of it."
	set {aff_liesel} += 2
	Lan (Smile): I wasn't planning to try.
- "Then you're on the hook for my medical bills."
	set {aff_liesel} += 1
	Lan (Smug): Then you're on the hook for my medical bills.
	Liesel (Smug): I'll bill you in ginger candy.
set {liesel_joined} = 1
The two of them walked back toward the dormitories together in a silence that had, somewhere over the last few weeks, stopped needing to be filled.
